  "description": "The supported entry point for Ably Pub/Sub in a server-side application - an ASP.NET or Azure host, a worker, a console app or any other backend the end user does not hold. Create clients through PubSubServer.CreateRealtimeClient(...) and PubSubServer.CreateHttpClient(...) in the Ably.PubSub.Server namespace; each accepts an API key, a ClientOptions or an Action<ClientOptions>, and returns the ordinary PubSubRealtimeClient or PubSubHttpClient so the whole of the Ably.PubSub API remains available. Server clients authenticate with an API key, or with a JWT that carries the signed server claim; Ably rejects any other token with error 40167. Creating a client any other way - including directly from the Ably.PubSub.Core implementation package this depends on - does not classify it as server-side, which Ably's platform behaviour and billing depend on. Install Ably.PubSub.Device instead in an end-user device application. See https://www.ably.com for more info.",
